    questionText: "Suppose \\( f(z) \\sim a_0 + \\dfrac{a_1}{z} + \\dfrac{a_2}{z^2} + \\cdots \\) as \\( z \\to \\infty \\) with \\( a_0 \\neq 0 \\). Show by induction (or otherwise) that \\( \\dfrac{1}{f(z)} \\sim \\dfrac{1}{a_0}\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} d_n z^{-n} \\), where \\( d_0 = 1 \\) and \\( \\sum_{k=0}^{n} d_{n-k} a_k = 0 \\) for \\( n \\ge 1 \\).",
