    questionText: "As \\( z \\to \\infty \\), \\( f(z) \\sim 1 + \\dfrac{1}{z} + \\dfrac{1}{2z^2} + \\dfrac{1}{6z^3} + \\cdots = e^{1/z} \\) and \\( g(z) \\sim 1 - \\dfrac{1}{z} + \\dfrac{1}{2z^2} - \\dfrac{1}{6z^3} + \\cdots = e^{-1/z} \\). (a) Compute the first four Cauchy coefficients \\( c_0,\\dots,c_3 \\) of \\( fg \\). (b) Verify they are consistent with \\( fg = 1 \\).",
